                <pb facs="0388" n="290" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg290"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum handed to Acting Secretary Hill by the
                        Chinese Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chinese Legation</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-09-10"><hi rendition="#italic">September 10,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">Cablegram from Earl Li Hung Chang,
                        dated the 7th September, 1900, transmitted by the Chinese minister at St.
                        Petersburg under date of the 9th September and received by Minister Wu on
                        the last-named date.</hi></p>
                <p>I am in receipt of an imperial edict of the 30th day of the seventh month (August
                    24, 1900), transmitted by way of Paoting Fu. It is as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Li Hung Chang, envoy plenipotentiary, is hereby vested with full
                            discretionary powers, and he shall promptly deal with whatever questions
                            may require attention. From this distance we will not control his
                            actions. Let this edict be forwarded with extra expedition at the rate
                            of 600 li per day (to Earl Li) for his information and guidance. Respect
                            this.</p>
                    </quote></p>
            </div>
        </body>
